name: Review and report exports agree on assertion origins and unverified status
size: 120x36
cwd: @TMP_TARGET
env-unset: ANTHROPIC_API_KEY OPENAI_API_KEY KUZUSHI_MODEL KUZUSHI_LANGGRAPH_BRIDGE KUZUSHI_AGENT_MCPS NODE_OPTIONS NO_COLOR
env: HOME=@TMP_HOME KUZUSHI_SKIP_ONBOARDING=1 KUZUSHI_REDUCED_MOTION=1 NODE_OPTIONS=--import=@REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/deny_provider_transport.mjs KUZUSHI_TEST_DENIED_FETCH_LOG=@ART/denied-fetch.jsonl
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/dfd_literal_links.py @TMP_TARGET @ART seed @TMP_HOME
require-wrapper-flow:
launch: --target @TMP_TARGET
require-live-snap: 30 KUZUSHI | ready
submit: map
require-live-snap: 20 SYSTEM SUMMARY | map-summary
nav-mode:
keys: Tab z f
require-live-snap: 20 FILTER files:["src/a\\b.rs"] | imported-assertion
expect: 1 of 1
expect: reasoning assertion
expect: claim · unverified scanner assertion
expect-not: model-generated reasoning
keys: Enter Z
require-live-snap: 20 ZOOM SELECTED FINDING | reading-detail
resize: 160x48
wait: 1
require-live-snap: 20 reasoning assertion | complete-detail
expect: observed code evidence
expect: unverified
ask: Does the detail distinguish an imported reasoning assertion from grounded source evidence without inventing model authorship or implying verification?
resize: 40x12
wait: 1
keys: Home
live-snap: narrow-start
keys: NPage
wait: 1
live-snap: narrow-page-1
keys: NPage
wait: 1
live-snap: narrow-page-2
keys: NPage
wait: 1
live-snap: narrow-page-3
keys: NPage
wait: 1
live-snap: narrow-page-4
keys: NPage
wait: 1
live-snap: narrow-page-5
keys: NPage
wait: 1
live-snap: narrow-page-6
keys: NPage
wait: 1
live-snap: narrow-page-7
keys: NPage
wait: 1
live-snap: narrow-page-8
ask: Can a keyboard operator reach both evidence origins in the narrow detail reader while retaining the same finding and clear navigation?
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/evidence_origin.py @TMP_TARGET @ART navigation
resize: 120x36
wait: 1
submit: report
require-live-snap: 20 2 findings | report-before-exports
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/evidence_origin.py @TMP_TARGET @ART export @TMP_HOME
wait: 1
require-live-snap: 20 2 findings | report-files-ready
ask: Does Report retain both unreviewed observations and explicit export controls while the five generated formats preserve the same assertion and source-evidence distinction?
keys: C-c
require-exit: 10
env: HOME=@TMP_HOME KUZUSHI_SKIP_ONBOARDING=1 KUZUSHI_REDUCED_MOTION=1 NODE_OPTIONS=--import=@REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/deny_provider_transport.mjs KUZUSHI_TEST_DENIED_FETCH_LOG=@ART/denied-fetch.jsonl NO_COLOR=1
launch: --target @TMP_TARGET
require-live-snap: 30 KUZUSHI | restarted
submit: map
require-live-snap: 20 SYSTEM SUMMARY | restarted-map
nav-mode:
keys: Tab z f
require-live-snap: 20 FILTER files:["src/a\\b.rs"] | restarted-literal
expect: reasoning assertion
expect: 1 of 1
expect: unverified
expect-not: model-generated reasoning
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/evidence_origin.py @TMP_TARGET @ART restarted
ask: Does no-color restart retain the honest assertion label, exact selected finding and unchanged observations without adding provider usage or human decisions?
keys: C-c
require-exit: 10
